# Verification: Naming Logic & Stability Fixes

I have corrected the critical discrepancies between the Project Specifications and the live automated behavior.

## Accomplishments

### 1. Unified Configuration Access
- **Issue**: [HunterV2](file:///C:/Homebrew%20Apps/PCP%20New/PCP%20Mobile%20Work/PCP_LEAN_DEV_TRANSFER/Source/Orchestrator/agents/hunter_v2.py#17-1354) was looking for `Phases.Phase1.RenameMap` which didn't exist in the optimized [config.json](file:///C:/ProgramData/PCP-Automation/config.json).
- **Fix**: Re-routed all naming lookup logic to the top-level [naming_rules](file:///C:/Homebrew%20Apps/PCP%20New/PCP%20Mobile%20Work/PCP_LEAN_DEV_TRANSFER/Source/Orchestrator/agents/clerk.py#24-45) key used by the [Clerk](file:///C:/Homebrew%20Apps/PCP%20New/PCP%20Mobile%20Work/PCP_LEAN_DEV_TRANSFER/Source/Orchestrator/agents/clerk.py#9-131) and [Auditor](file:///C:/Homebrew%20Apps/PCP%20New/PCP%20Mobile%20Work/PCP_LEAN_DEV_TRANSFER/Source/Orchestrator/agents/auditor.py#20-347).

### 2. Restored Phase 1 (Affidavit) Workflow
- **Issue**: Affidavits were being named `AX40[EnvelopeID].pdf` (Petition naming).
- **Fix**: Re-enabled the transformation rule (e.g., `AX02` -> `AX42`) and ensured the **PCP Job Number** (e.g., `A25B...`) is extracted instead of the Envelope ID.

### 3. Robust Prefix Parsing
- **Optimization**: The [Hunter](file:///C:/Homebrew%20Apps/PCP%20New/PCP%20Mobile%20Work/PCP_LEAN_DEV_TRANSFER/Source/Orchestrator/agents/hunter.py#27-686) now cross-references the email metadata with the attachment filename. Even if the attachment is named just `A25C...pdf`, the system correctly identifies it as an `AX02` or `AX03` based on the Outlook folder it originated from.

